From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mason Morris <masonmorris8@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Leave the HRTF database to the panner that needs it

An online context pre-created the built-in HRTF sphere for every sample
rate, which costs a second or more while the context is made and only
serves panners when the embedder set no Chromium responses. The host
always sets them, so the load was dead work at every context start, and
its cost showed up as currentTime already partway through when a page
first read it. Panners still load either database on first use.
---
 src/context/concrete_base.rs | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/context/concrete_base.rs b/src/context/concrete_base.rs
index 014cd13..4d713c6 100644
--- a/src/context/concrete_base.rs
+++ b/src/context/concrete_base.rs
@@ -216,11 +216,6 @@ impl ConcreteBaseAudioContext {
             LISTENER_PARAM_IDS.end,
         );
 
-        // For an online AudioContext, pre-create the HRTF-database for panner nodes
-        if !offline {
-            crate::node::load_hrtf_processor(sample_rate as u32);
-        }
-
         base
     }
 
